# Part 1: Basic Meta-Analysis

- Compute the effect sizes (SMD in this activity)

- Fit a fixed-effects model.

- Fit a random-effects model.

- Fit a meta-regression with a categorical moderator.

```{r}
library(metafor)
dat_smd <- escalc(measure = "SMD",
                  m1i = m1i,
                  m2i = m2i,
                  sd1i = sd1i,
                  sd2i = sd2i,
                  n1i = n1i,
                  n2i = n2i,
                  data = dat)
head(dat_smd)
```


```{r}

#Fit a Fixed-Effects Model
fe_model <- rma(yi = yi, vi = vi, data = dat_smd, method = "FE", slab = id)
summary(fe_model)
forest(fe_model,
       mlab = "Fixed-Effects Model",
       main = "Fixed-Effects Meta-Analysis")
```

```{r}
# Fit a Random-Effects Model
re_model <- rma(yi = yi, vi = vi, data = dat_smd, method = "REML", slab = id)
summary(re_model)
forest(re_model,
       mlab = "Random-Effects Model",
       main = "Random-Effects Meta-Analysis")
```

```{r}
#Fit a Meta-Regression with Moderator
meta_reg_model <- rma(yi ~ cond, vi = vi, data = dat_smd, method = "REML", slab = id)
summary(meta_reg_model)
forest(meta_reg_model,
       mlab = "Mixed-Effects Model",
       main = "Meta-Regression with Moderator")
```

